Every text stands in a fenced block whose first line is `[[TEXT <id>]]`; the text is every line after the id line up to the closing fence, joined by line feeds, no line feed at its end. Its length and sha256 (UTF-8, unfilled) are in THE FROZEN TABLE; **check every one BEFORE filling; a difference is a STOP.** Fill-ins are `<<NAME>>`, replaced by program only; **no `<<` may remain in anything you write.** `<<WRITE-DATE>>` is `date +%Y-%m-%d` at the write; `<<HHMM>>` the clock of the history write from `date`, once, as `HH:MM`. `<<C-82>>` is P-7's. `<<OWED-SHARED>>` and `<<OWED-CLAUDEMD>>` are the highest owed number of the live `BACKLOG.md` plus 1 and plus 2 (113 and 114 at drafting; PREDICTED). `<<FILE-1>>` to `<<FILE-4>>` are, for the four staged copies in THE DESIGN FILES order, `<name>: <size> bytes, last saved <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS> AEDT, sha256 <64 hex>` (size and saved time by `stat` of the staged copy, which `cp -p` kept equal to the live file's; at drafting the first would read `02_architecture.docx: 164538 bytes, last saved 2026-11-24 08:38:52 AEDT, sha256 ed8e2bdfd716ddfd932e8d6224bf9139c041ed7b801551c166c951d5bbe4fbc9`). `<<REF-KEY>>` is T-R's key from your write log. `<<ATTACH-COUNT>>` is the count of attachments read back on T-R as a word (`four`), `<<ATTACH-LIST>>` their file names joined by `, `. `<<ACTIONS-CREATED>>` is `<n> tickets created: ` followed by `<label> <key>` for each create of T-A1 to T-A6 in T-order, joined by `, ` (labels: THE JIRA TABLE's last column), or `no ticket created`; `<<ACTIONS-SKIPPED>>` is `No create was skipped: before each create a search for its summary found no issue holding it` or `Skipped as already present (an issue holding the same summary): ` followed by `<label> <key>` for each skip, joined by `, `. `<<CLOSED-LIST>>` is the keys of T-C1 to T-C4 that read Done at the end of 4e, as English (`OXPD2-33, OXPD2-39, OXPD2-41 and OXPD2-47`), each moved by this pass or named in STATUS as found Done already. **This kit holds