## PART 2: JIRA (slot JIRA WRITE; the SECOND write of Step 4, after `CLARIFICATIONS.md`, before `BACKLOG.md`)
**The one shape of every create** (your helper builds it from THE JIRA TABLE and the frozen texts; THE JIRA FENCE refuses any other): `POST /rest/api/3/issue` with the JSON body
`{"fields": {"project": {"key": "OXPD2"}, "issuetype": {"id": "10030"}, "summary": <S text>, "description": <ADF of the filled D text>, "assignee": {"accountId": "616503d4bfa2c1006b1971d1"}, "labels": [<label>], "duedate": <due>}, "update": {"issuelinks": [{"add": {"type": {"id": "10003"}, "outwardIssue": {"key": "OXPD2-1"}}}]}}`
where `<label>` and `<due>` are THE JIRA TABLE's; a row whose due reads `none` carries NO `duedate` key (six `fields` keys, not seven).
**The ADF of a D text** (by program, never by hand; the rule of B2030, which read back 29 of 29 EQUAL): split the filled text on `\n\n` into blocks; a block whose every line starts with `>` is ONE `blockquote` node whose `paragraph` children are its lines split on lines equal to `>`, each line with its leading `> ` removed (every quoted group of this kit is one line); any other block is ONE `paragraph` node holding ONE `text` node with the block's text (every such block of this kit is one line). No marks, no other node. **The inverse** (for the read-back): a `paragraph` gives its text nodes joined; a `blockquote` gives `> ` plus each child paragraph's text, joined by `\n>\n`; nodes are joined by `\n\n`; any other node type is UNEQUAL.
**THE SKIP RULE (each create; idempotent by summary; inside the same process):** (a) search `project = OXPD2 AND ( labels = "<its label>" )` and GET each hit's summary; (b) the project reader's phrase search for the S text (`text ~ "\"<summary>\""`, the reader softens it only on a non-200); (c) if any issue of (a) or (b) holds a summary EQUAL to the S text, byte for byte: SKIP this T-id, write `{"kind": "skip", "t": <T-id>, "key": <key>}` to the write log, create nothing; (d) if (b) returns a key that is neither equal nor one this pass created: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira near-duplicate <T-id> <key>` (no create); (e) else create. **After a create:** HTTP 201 and a key `OXPD2-<n>`; write `{"kind": "create", "t": <T-id>, "key": <key>, "clock": <date>}` to the write log at once; then GET `issue/<key>?fields=summary,description,assignee,duedate,labels,issuelinks,issuetype,status,project,attachment` and check: summary EQUAL; the inverse of the description EQUAL to the filled D text; assignee account id `616503d4bfa2c1006b1971d1`; duedate as the table (null where `none`); labels exactly `[<label>]`; issue type id `10030`; project `OXPD2`; exactly one issue link, type `Relates`, to `OXPD2-1`; a one-character mutant of the summary UNEQUAL (control). Write `{"kind": "verify", ...}`. **A T-R found by THE SKIP RULE (a successor's run) is used as `<<REF-KEY>>` only if its description's inverse EQUALS the R-D text filled with THIS run's `<<FILE-n>>`; else `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira T-R exists with other files`.**
**THE UPLOADS (T-U1 to T-U4, after T-R's verify; one file each, in THE DESIGN FILES order):** first GET `issue/<<REF-KEY>>?fields=attachment`: an attachment with the same file name AND size is a SKIP for that file (write `{"kind": "skip-upload", ...}`); the same name with another size is a STOP. Then D-3, then `POST /rest/api/3/issue/<<REF-KEY>>/attachments` as `multipart/form-data` with ONE part, field name `file`, its filename the file's own name and its bytes the staged copy's (sha256 re-checked in-process against its `<<FILE-n>>` fill just before the request), headers `X-Atlassian-Token: no-check` and `Accept: application/json`, authorised exactly as the project reader's `real_transport` authorises (its `env()` read in-process; nothing printed). **The project reader has no multipart path** (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: `b1785.py` holds no `multipart`, `attachments` or `no-check`, and no other `.tools/` helper sends one): your helper builds this ONE transport, and THE JIRA FENCE admits it only for that path. Expect HTTP 200 and a JSON list of ONE attachment whose `filename` equals the name and `size` equals the staged size; write `{"kind": "upload", "t": <T-U id>, "id": <attachment id>, "filename": ..., "size": ..., "sha256": ...}` at once. **After the four:** GET `issue/<<REF-KEY>>?fields=attachment`: exactly four attachments, their names exactly the four, each size equal to its staged copy's; GET `attachment/<id>` for each: `filename` and `size` equal (write `{"kind": "verify-upload", ...}`). Space every POST at least 3.2 s from the one before.
**THE CLOSE RULE (T-C1 to T-C4: OXPD2-33, OXPD2-39, OXPD2-41, OXPD2-47, in that order; slot JIRA WRITE):** for each: GET `issue/<key>?fields=summary,status,assignee,labels,duedate,issuelinks,comment,resolution` and save it as the before-snapshot; its summary must EQUAL THE JIRA FACTS' line for it; status `10022` Done: SKIP (write `{"kind": "skip-close", ...}`, name it in STATUS); status `10052` Backlog: go on; any other status: STOP. GET `issue/<key>/transitions`: exactly one transition with id `41`, whose `to.id` is `10022` and `to.name` is `Done`, `hasScreen` false; else STOP. Then `POST /rest/api/3/issue/<key>/transitions` with the body exactly `{"transition": {"id": "41"}}` (no `fields`, no `update`, no comment): expect HTTP 204; write `{"kind": "close", "t": <T-C id>, "key": <key>, "clock": <date>}` at once; then GET the same fields again and check: status id `10022`, status category `done`; summary, assignee account id, labels, due date, the issue-link ids and the comment total each EQUAL to the before-snapshot (control: a before-snapshot with one label changed reads UNEQUAL); print the resolution as Jira set it (the workflow's, not yours). Write `{"kind": "verify-close", ...}`.
**Any answer but the expected code, a time-out, or a read-back that is not EQUAL: STOP at once** (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira <T-id> <what>`); after a non-expected answer or a time-out, run that request's own idempotency read FIRST (THE SKIP RULE's (a) and (b) for a create; the attachment list for an upload; the status for a close) and name what it found: a POST may have landed without its answer. **Never retry a POST blindly; never edit, delete or comment anything.**
**THE JIRA FENCE (your helper refuses, by code, before any request leaves the process; each refusal is a selftest case that must fire):** any method but GET and POST; a POST to any path but `/rest/api/3/issue`, `/rest/api/3/issue/<<REF-KEY>>/attachments` (only once `<<REF-KEY>>` is in the write log as T-R's create or skip) and `/rest/api/3/issue/<K>/transitions` for K exactly one of `OXPD2-33`, `OXPD2-39`, `OXPD2-41`, `OXPD2-47`; a create body whose keys are not exactly `fields` and `update`, whose `fields` keys are not exactly those above for its row, or any value outside the shape above; a transition body other than exactly `{"transition": {"id": "41"}}`; an upload with more or fewer than one part, a file name outside the four, bytes whose sha256 is not its `<<FILE-n>>` fill, a size over the upload limit; a T-id not in THE JIRA TABLE or already done or skipped in the write log; a POST out of the order T-R, T-U1 to T-U4, T-A1 to T-A6, T-C1 to T-C4; an 8th create, a 5th upload, a 5th transition; a summary or description not EQUAL to its frozen text (sha256 of the S and unfilled D texts against THE FROZEN TABLE); a text whose `scan_jira` codes differ from THE JIRA TABLE's codes column (a new code is a STOP; the codes that stand are named in THE JIRA TEXT RULE); a text holding the value of any key of the project's `.env` (checked in-process, never printed; control: a planted value fires); the slot JIRA not WRITE; a file `.tools/b2034/HOLD` present; the clock at or after HARD STOP minus 10.
**THE JIRA TEXT RULE (the drafter's list over the project's own `scan_jira`; it is NOT the project's records rule).** The project's `scan_jira` (from `b1785.py`, loaded by `importlib`) is run on the summary and on each paragraph of the ADF (each `\n\n` block, a quoted block with its `> `); the codes it prints for each T-id, on the FILLED texts, must EQUAL THE JIRA TABLE's codes column. The codes that stand, and why each is accepted: `S-NAME` (the tickets are addressed to the product owner by his name, as he asked, and quote his words, which name people); `S-DQUOTE` (his words are quoted); `S-WORD:lane` (T-A4 only: "swim lane diagrams" in his w8 words). Never standing: `S-CARD`, `S-URL`, `S-BNUM`, `S-BTICK`, `S-NEWLINE`, `S-ASCII`, `S-PLACEHOLDER` (R-D unfilled holds its fills; filled, it holds none), and every `S-WORD` other than `lane` (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: none of them fires on any of the 14 texts; the R-D text filled with the drafter's prototype values fires `S-NAME` only).

